# Each line says why it is here (standing rule).
# CONFIG_ENV_SIZE, CONFIG_PARTITION_TYPE_GUID, CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC: the
#   environment lives in the empty `uboot-env` partition found by its GUID
#   (family.toml), so the built-in environment boots from the microSD (MMC).
# CONFIG_ENV_REDUNDANT, CONFIG_ENV_SIZE=0x8000: two copies of the environment,
#   so a power cut during a write leaves the other copy (the slot record lives
#   there: default, trial, trial_attempts). Two copies of 0x8000 fit the 128 KiB
#   partition with room to grow. It was one copy of 0x10000 until PR B28.
# CONFIG_OF_CONTROL: U-Boot looks for the environment partition by type GUID
#   only when it is built with device-tree control (env/mmc.c).
# CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE is not set: undoes the default that would drop the env.
# CONFIG_TOOLS_MKEFICAPSULE is not set: its PKCS#11 signing needs a GnuTLS built
#   with p11-kit, which Buildroot's host-gnutls is not (dev's note; the tool is
#   not used by Atlas).
# MOVES AT THE LEMNOS L2 MOVE: the environment lines below (ENV_SIZE, ENV_REDUNDANT, OF_CONTROL,
#   PARTITION_TYPE_GUID, ENV_IS_NOWHERE, ENV_IS_IN_MMC) will be written by `lemnos-ctl tree --uboot-config`
#   from the board file and included by Gaia; this fragment then keeps only board hardware lines.
# Z2 (the bench slot form, HARD RULE of 2026-11-14): the environment is on the SD card, which is U-Boot's mmc 1 on this
#   family (mmc 0 is the disabled eMMC node), and the raw-offset fallback is off. Values as Gaia's rk-env branch sets them
#   (examples/boards/rk35xx/assets/u-boot.fragment at 1db105c): CONFIG_ENV_SIZE=0x10000 is Lemnos's uboot_env_size
#   (testing/boards/rk3566-slots.toml at e2e45ce7), the copy size of the 128 KiB uboot-env partition in family.toml.
#   CONFIG_ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=1 and CONFIG_ENV_MMC_USE_DT=y are the same rule: without USE_DT the redundant copies fall back
#   to the offsets over the partition table (env/mmc.c:194-202). Lemnos's generator does not write USE_DT (its
#   --uboot-config output lists ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX only), so this file adds it. The check (scripts/check-devices.sh,
#   rk35xx_env_rule) refuses a slot image whose config lacks either line.
CONFIG_ENV_SIZE=0x10000
CONFIG_ENV_REDUNDANT=y
CONFIG_ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=1
CONFIG_ENV_MMC_USE_DT=y
CONFIG_OF_CONTROL=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TYPE_GUID=y
# CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE is not set
CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC=y
# CONFIG_ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=1 and CONFIG_ENV_MMC_USE_DT=y (PR G12): the environment is on the SD (mmc 1; mmc 0 is the eMMC
#   socket), and U-Boot's raw-offset fallback is off, so it saves nowhere else. Gaia's rk35xx example (u-boot.fragment, rk-env
#   #150, c0d084f) has the same two lines; the coordinator's 2026-11-14 hard rule requires them on every RK slot image.
CONFIG_ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=1
CONFIG_ENV_MMC_USE_DT=y
# CONFIG_TOOLS_MKEFICAPSULE is not set

# The boot path's options (Z2): the lines Lemnos's `lemnos-ctl tree --uboot-config` writes for a `record = "uboot"` board
# (service/ctl/src/boot_dir.rs uboot_config, at Lemnos pr/BB1b e2e45ce7; its test the_uboot_config_fragment_names_what_the_boot_path_needs
# lists them). Each is U-Boot v2026.10's name, as Lemnos checked it against the Kconfig files (testing/board-runs/I5i7.md).
#   The boot script (packaging/uboot/boot.cmd): hush with while and for, sysboot, fdt, sleep, saveenv, and the FAT boot partition.
#   The fastboot gadget on USB (the pause and the offer for flashing) and the watchdog the loop services (cmd/fastboot.c:115).
CONFIG_CMD_SAVEENV=y
CONFIG_EFI_PARTITION=y
CONFIG_HUSH_PARSER=y
CONFIG_CMD_FDT=y
CONFIG_CMD_SLEEP=y
CONFIG_CMD_SYSBOOT=y
CONFIG_USB_GADGET=y
CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_FASTBOOT=y
CONFIG_CMD_FASTBOOT=y
CONFIG_FASTBOOT_USB_DEV=0
CONFIG_FASTBOOT_FLASH=y
CONFIG_FASTBOOT_FLASH_MMC=y
CONFIG_FASTBOOT_FLASH_MMC_DEV=0
CONFIG_WDT=y
CONFIG_WATCHDOG=y
CONFIG_WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART=y
# CONFIG_SPL_ROCKCHIP_BACK_TO_BROM (B31): the SPL checks the boot-mode register at its first instruction and returns to
#   the BootROM's download mode when it holds BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD (0xEF08A53C; bootrom.c:46-59 and :72-73). That is the
#   value a board's `reboot loader` writes (the reboot-mode node, boards/radxa-rock-4d/assets/dts). Without this line
#   bootrom.c is not compiled: the RK3566/RK3576 defconfigs select neither TPL nor this option (only the RK3066, RK3188
#   and RV1126 select it: arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig:50,87,551), so the register is never read by the SPL. Selects
#   ROCKCHIP_BROM_HELPER and SPL_BOOTROM_SUPPORT. UNVERIFIED on a board.
CONFIG_SPL_ROCKCHIP_BACK_TO_BROM=y
